WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.650
So Ra No Wo To

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:50.210
I'll have you practice with only
the mouthpiece for a while.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:52.670
Any problem with that?

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.720
No! But, umm...

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:00.780
I want to be able to play songs like you...

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.720
I won't make it easy for you.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.020
I'm ready for anything!

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.960
It's breakfast time.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.230
The mess hall is over there.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.230
Get going.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.350
Right!

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.100
It's rough and ragged.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.910
Nice to meet you.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.680
Good morning!

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.740
You suck!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:06.950
First Battle -
A Chair Story

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:21.170
Actually, we prepared it to
welcome you last night.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.510
A little treat for you.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:25.330
Thank you!

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.970
Oh, Rio.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.210
Did you bring in the fish
I was drying upstairs?

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.080
No, not me.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.590
That's odd...

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.530
Come on, Noël.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.820
You can sleep after breakfast!

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.800
I'll do my best...

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.860
That's not doing your best.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.270
I'm doing my best...

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.790
That's Rio-sempai's...

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.980
Sit down.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:01.800
Breakfast will get cold.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:15.790
Let me reintroduce you to
everyone in the 1121 Platoon.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.970
First, the captain.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.470
Lieutenant Filicia Heidemann.
I'm a tank commander.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.240
Let's have fun while you're here!

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.740
Nice to meet you.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.710
This is...

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.780
Hey, Noël.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.500
Noël Kannagi...

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.180
Corporal Kannagi.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.390
Pilot.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.490
She's our mechanic, too.

00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:57.860
Nice to meet you.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.490
And finally...

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.320
Private Kureha Suminoya.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.720
I'm the gunner.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.450
Listen.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:17.120
I'm younger than you, but I've been here
longer, so you'd better do as I-

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:24.040
She collapsed.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.540
Thank you for everything, Noël-chan.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.860
OK, let's get to breakfast.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:35.580
But...

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:39.330
Enough!

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.570
All right! Then let's eat.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.740
Let's eat.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:50.660
I'm so happy...

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.120
I cut the bacon myself.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.530
Eat all you want.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:55.660
OK!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.380
Soldiers and trumpeters
both need stamina.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.670
Eat a lot and grow strong.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.990
I'll do my best.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:15.760
Kureha.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:18.230
Y-Yes?

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:21.960
Once breakfast is over,
show her around the base.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:27.440
Roger.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:32.740
Attention!

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:39.500
Actually, I'm really busy,
but it was an order,

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.260
so I'm showing you around
because I have to!

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.660
R-Right. Thank you, Kureha-san.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:48.880
Don't be so informal, Private Sorami!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:49.910
I'm sorry!

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:53.410
Uh, Private Suminoya-dono.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:57.960
Fine.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.480
Then first, face the platoon and national flags...

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.300
Salute!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:10.060
The 1121 Platoon presently
consists of five members:

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:18.230
A lieutenant, a sergeant, a corporal,
and two privates. Five in total.

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:21.000
Yes, Private Suminoya-dono.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.420
That's the absolute minimum
required for a platoon. So...

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.670
That means we're all elites.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.920
Understood!

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.750
Our platoon has been given
the following armaments:

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:37.220
One tank,

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.960
one heavy machine gun,

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:40.790
two light machine guns,

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.570
four rifles,

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.210
five handguns.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:51.720
Using these, our mission is to defend the
national border around Seize, Trois.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:52.810
Um...

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.900
P-Private Suminoya-dono!

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.470
I have a question!

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.650
Very well.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:04.540
Permission to speak granted, Private Sorami.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:10.800
If, uh... If my memory is correct,
beyond Seize is...

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:14.850
Correct. Beyond the mountains
is a no man's land.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:20.830
But the borders of Helvetia only extend this far,
so this is a national border!

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.060
The front lines!

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.190
An important base!

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.680
So we always keep watch.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:28.950
The five of us,
throughout the night.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:30.820
Sleeping during watch is
absolutely forbidden.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:36.570
This is the only hotline in the city
that's connected to the Capitol.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.310
Which means...

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:42.770
If it rings, something big
is about to happen.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:47.670
If it does, everyone's woken up
and put on alert.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:48.520
Got it?

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:51.170
Yes, Private Suminoya-dono!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.650
The second floor contains the captain's
quarters and the briefing room.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.010
Under normal circumstances, entry is...

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.340
Well, it's perfectly all right.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.240
But make sure you knock first!

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.070
This is the latrine.

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:26.080
Bath drawing and cleaning duties
are assigned by rotation. And...

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.280
Bathing is done in order
of rank, right?

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:35.470
No.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.540
It's more fun if we all
bathe together.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.370
Captain!

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.120
What are you doing?

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:43.400
Cleaning the bathroom.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.600
But it's Noël's turn!

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.750
But she seemed so tired.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:53.990
You'll set a bad example
for the rookie!

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.650
I'll do it later.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.910
You just go sit somewhere and
act captain-ish for a while!

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:21.180
OK, take a good look!

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:26.050
This is the 1121st's
main battle tank.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:29.660
Vector-Type Zero Autonomous
Tank Walker, the Takemikazuchi.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:31.980
It's much bigger than the one
at the training grounds!

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.990
This is one of the so-called
zero-generation tanks.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:42.700
It's a relic from the past.
There are fewer than ten left in the country.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:46.370
I've heard of them.
They're supposed to be really amazing.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.400
But its legs...

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.630
It's undergoing repair.
There aren't enough parts.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:11:01.320
O-OK, so there's no manual either,
and we can't even find most of the parts.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:05.390
But Noël will take care
of it somehow, OK?

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:08.300
Don't you dare call it useless!

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:15.750
I'm sure someday it will...

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.900
Don't make fun of us...

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.990
I know we're lax.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:27.070
We're lax as heck.

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:30.830
They call us the useless Seize squad
or say we're just for decoration.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:34.420
We're a pink squad,
yet we don't even have a working tank.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:35.430
But...!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.170
Kureha-chan.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:39.810
That's it for your tour!

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:40.550
Dismissed!

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:45.420
Sounds like they're getting along.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:47.060
Are they?

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:50.560
Just like we did, when we met.

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:53.120
You're right.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.540
But it's a bit of a problem.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:12:00.070
After I sent you after Kana-chan last night...

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:04.070
Captain, why is she communications?

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:09.010
You said the new recruit was going
to be a loader or a pilot!

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.480
It's not up to us.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:13.640
Command sent her.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:16.130
In the army, you don't always
get what you want.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.470
But...!

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.670
There, there. It's all right.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:25.660
Rio will take care of you, too,
just as she always has.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.410
And of course, so will I.

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:36.960
She's got pretty good intuition,
so she may have realized something.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.950
You think?

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:42.370
We have to do something.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.330
I saw it.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:50.830
Saw what?

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:05.380
A ghost?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.010
Yeah.

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:14.730
No way.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.790
You were just tired
and seeing things.

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:18.610
I thought so.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.470
What do you mean,
you thought so?

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:21.950
I saw it, too.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:22.700
The ghost.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.400
It was in the barracks, right?

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.110
Yeah.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:30.190
Don't encourage her!

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.120
But there's nothing special
about ghosts, right?

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:36.190
Stop it, I said!

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:38.590
And you, too, Noël!

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:42.800
You're an engineer.
Go investigate like one and then report back!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:43.420
No.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.810
Why?

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:46.630
Scared.

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:48.450
What are you saying?!

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.050
There are no ghosts!

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:52.640
There aren't! There aren't!
There aren't! There aren't!

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:03.070
I agree with you.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:04.440
Yeah.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.450
Yes. There are no ghosts.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:07.210
There aren't!

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:08.280
Not at all!

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.590
Not a chance!

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:10.150
All right!

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.440
Give the place a thorough investigation.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:18.320
Blow your trumpet if you
encounter the enemy.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:20.370
We'll send reinforcements!

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.320
Why?

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:27.610
Um, Private-dono...

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:30.760
What is it, Kana... Private!

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:34.270
This is kinda fun, isn't it?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.850
The lightning sounds like
a marching beat.

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:43.030
This is a mission!

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.680
It's not a game.

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:47.460
Listen, Kana... Private Sorami!

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:48.570
You're on point.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:49.850
I'll back you up.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:50.700
Right!

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.030
Advance!

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:10.510
This place has stayed the way
it was before it was a fort.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.510
What was it before?

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.040
How am I supposed to know?

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.590
Get going!

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:18.510
OK.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:45.650
Ideographs.

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.090
I wonder what it says.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:50.680
You can't read it, so put it down.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:53.050
It'd be wonderful
if I could read it.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:56.240
It's probably some
junk from long ago.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.220
Let's get going.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.720
You're not scared?

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:06.570
Nope.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.300
Idiot!

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:13.590
But ghosts protect us, right?

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:14.710
What?

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:20.810
In the village where I was born, we had an annual
festival to celebrate and thank the ghosts.

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.790
Where in the middle of nowhere
were you born?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:31.400
You see, ghosts possess people, drink their blood,
move corpses, and lots of nasty stuff like that.

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.620
That was close.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:50.990
Sometimes rats carry
bad diseases...

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.150
What?

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.110
So, you are scared...

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:05.320
Is it gone?

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:06.870
I think so.

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:15.680
Hey, Kureha.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.010
Private-dono.

00:17:23.030 --> 00:17:27.310
I was thinking...
Maybe this was a school.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:28.850
What?

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:34.760
There's no school this size,
even in the Capitol.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:38.820
But there used to be a lot
more people, right?

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:44.440
So I'm sure, in this school,
there were a bunch of kids our age.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:46.540
They all studied together...

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.620
What? What?

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:50.460
What!

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:53.120
I'm sure they taught music here!

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:55.290
Outside the army?

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.410
Look!

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:01.390
It hasn't changed.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:05.810
I can't read the words, but...

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:12.150
D-sharp.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:15.150
The sounds don't change...

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:37.340
What are you standing there for?

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.620
Wh-What?!

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:40.180
Hey, Kureha-chan!

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.170
It's wonderful, isn't it?

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:42.140
What is?

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.050
All of it!

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:44.180
Huh?

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:51.060
The town of Seize, this building,
everyone in our platoon... They're all...!

00:18:54.580 --> 00:19:00.470
We're just a useless troop
in the middle of nowhere.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.620
Our tank doesn't work,

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:07.000
and they forget to supply
us a lot of the time.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:09.740
We never get any real missions.

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:11.730
We're all so lax...

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:14.460
But you love it, don't you?

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:25.680
What? What? What?!

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.760
I-I-It's here!

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:30.770
Wait, Kureha!

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.690
Kanata!

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:49.490
Amazing.

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:51.080
Of course it is!

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:57.090
I'm the gunner of the 1121st,
and it's a wonderful place,

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:59.350
and I love it more than anything!

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.850
So that's our ghost, huh?

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:12.010
How do you mistake
this for a ghost?

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:16.660
Hey, you.

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:19.580
You look a lot like that
thief from yesterday.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:24.630
Why, you... You're tonight's dinner!

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:28.240
You mustn't frighten her
when she's hurt, Rio.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.510
But...

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:33.710
I'm sure she has no place else to go.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:37.710
And what's our symbol?

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.470
It wouldn't be right to cook her.

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:44.910
Isn't that right, Shuko-chan?

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:46.520
She <i>named</i> it?

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:49.650
But I think it's wonderful.

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:53.420
Yesterday, you almost died,
thanks to this thing.

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:57.430
But today, thanks to it, I was able
to have a great adventure!

00:20:57.430 --> 00:20:59.480
Right, Kureha-chan?

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.490
What are you talking about?

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:05.490
You couldn't even classify that
as a <i>little</i> adventure!

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.490
Sheesh. I guess majority rule wins here.

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:11.130
No.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.910
Captain's orders.

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:14.960
But next time you steal food,

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:16.500
you'll be punished.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.890
Got it?

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:04.100
That was Rio this morning, wasn't it?

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:08.370
We'd start getting complaints from the
town if Kanata did it every day.

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:09.600
I'm sorry.

00:22:15.760 --> 00:22:17.600
That's your seat.

00:22:23.770 --> 00:22:25.110
Kureha-chan?

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:29.550
I just happened to find
